WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:01.693
How are ya?

00:00:01.693 --> 00:00:02.526
I'm good.

00:00:02.526 --> 00:00:03.520
You know how to light up a room.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.353
It's very nice.
Aww!

00:00:04.353 --> 00:00:05.186
Thanks for being here.

00:00:05.186 --> 00:00:06.019
You're always sweet!

00:00:06.019 --> 00:00:06.852
(audience cheers)

00:00:06.852 --> 00:00:07.685
[Conan] Thank you. It's very nice.

00:00:07.685 --> 00:00:08.548
I haven't seen you in a long time.

00:00:08.548 --> 00:00:09.737
Oh! Thanks for being here!

00:00:09.737 --> 00:00:12.068
You know, we actually haven't talked

00:00:12.068 --> 00:00:14.080
since Friends went off the air.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.830
And it's so strange because
it's been eighteen months.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:17.663
I don't know how you feel.

00:00:17.663 --> 00:00:19.940
That does not feel... it
doesn't feel like Friends

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.203
has been off the air for
eighteen months 'cause-

00:00:21.203 --> 00:00:22.036
I know.

00:00:22.036 --> 00:00:23.170
It's still on all the time.

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:24.830
Well, so it's really not
off the air, actually.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.850
Exactly, yeah, it's still
going and going strong.

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:28.683
Sorry.

00:00:28.683 --> 00:00:29.516
Yeah, it's okay.

00:00:29.516 --> 00:00:30.349
(audience laughs)

00:00:30.349 --> 00:00:31.182
No! People are... I mean, people watch it.

00:00:31.182 --> 00:00:32.015
People still love it.

00:00:32.015 --> 00:00:33.530
I think they're gonna be
watching that show for a long,

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:34.580
it's gonna be like the Honeymooners.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:35.750
It'll be on for a long time.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:36.660
Wow, yeah.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.493
Yeah, they're gonna start showing it

00:00:37.493 --> 00:00:38.587
in black and white for no reason.

00:00:38.587 --> 00:00:40.210
(laughing)

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:42.770
Do you find yourself passing
TVs every now and then

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.810
and the show is on and
do you ever watch it?

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.530
I do. Yeah, every once in a while.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:47.930
If I'm flipping through the channels

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:50.080
and I see it, I do stop watch it.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.440
It makes me happy. (audience laughs)

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.450
Oh, that's nice. That's really nice.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:55.140
It does. I miss it.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.020
You know, what's funny is
that when enough time goes by,

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.270
and this is true, you won't remember

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:00.560
what happens in an episode.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.393
No, that's true.

00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:02.930
So I'll get to watch it
sort of like you all did?

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:03.763
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.681
And you'll be like, "Oh,
what's gonna happen?"

00:01:05.681 --> 00:01:06.514
(Jennifer laughs)

00:01:06.514 --> 00:01:07.347
"And who's she? Wait!" (laughs)

00:01:07.347 --> 00:01:08.207
That's cause I get old and senile, right?

00:01:08.207 --> 00:01:09.970
"That's me."

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:11.870
You know, Lisa Kudrow was here

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:13.580
and she said, when the
show went off the air,

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.420
people were talking about
grabbing different stuff

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.380
and she grabbed the cookie jar-

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.213
She did.

00:01:18.213 --> 00:01:19.300
From the set that had
the little clock on it.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.860
And I'm curious, did you grab anything?

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.820
I didn't grab anything.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:25.120
Did I grab anything?

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:26.470
No, I didn't grab anything.

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:27.750
They all stole stuff.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:28.614
Right, yeah.

00:01:28.614 --> 00:01:29.447
(audience laughs)

00:01:29.447 --> 00:01:30.280
Yeah. They're all thieves.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:31.250
Yeah, people say like,
"Oh, I think I took this.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:32.500
I took that," that's called stealing.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:33.333
That's stealing. (audience chuckles)

00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:34.166
Yeah, that's wrong.

00:01:34.166 --> 00:01:35.690
But they felt like 10 years, I own this.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:36.720
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.520
Yeah. Like Matt LeBlanc said
he took a whole sectional

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.080
or something from the, you know?

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:42.950
Didn't he take foosball table?

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:44.390
I think he said he was gonna take it

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:45.873
but they stopped him when he
was going through the gate.

00:01:45.873 --> 00:01:46.706
They did?

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:47.539
Yeah. (chuckles)

00:01:47.539 --> 00:01:48.372
He was just like, "You can't have that."

00:01:48.372 --> 00:01:50.220
You know, it's funny. This
is a homecoming for you.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:51.270
You're from New York city.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:52.630
Yes!

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:53.463
You were raised here.

00:01:53.463 --> 00:01:55.167
I was raised here, 92nd and Columbus.

00:01:55.167 --> 00:01:56.000
(audience cheers)

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.191
That's nice.

00:01:57.191 --> 00:01:58.630
(audience clapping)

00:01:58.630 --> 00:01:59.860
Now you can give that address out.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:01.470
Now I can give that address out.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:02.303
No. But, yeah.

00:02:02.303 --> 00:02:03.136
But you had a good time?

00:02:03.136 --> 00:02:05.332
It's such a cool place to
grow up. I would think.

00:02:05.332 --> 00:02:06.670
Such a great place.
There's a lot of excitement.

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:08.330
Such a great place. It's so beautiful.

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:12.120
Just, you know, people on the
streets, all walks of life.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.880
I miss that, I do miss that.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:15.890
'Cause you know, LA you
get in a little bubble.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:16.723
[Conan] Right.

00:02:16.723 --> 00:02:18.170
You travel in the bubble
to your next bubble.

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:19.534
That's your choice to travel
in the a little bubble.

00:02:19.534 --> 00:02:21.280
Hey it's my... (laughing)

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.134
You should get a car.
Yeah, but it's fun.

00:02:22.134 --> 00:02:22.967
It's really fun in there.

00:02:22.967 --> 00:02:25.030
(audience laughing)

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:27.224
It's the new bubble, It's
what everyone's doing.

00:02:27.224 --> 00:02:28.057
Yeah.

00:02:28.057 --> 00:02:29.170
Do you, do you...

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.620
I heard a story that you
once slept outside of a hotel

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:33.510
here in New York city.
Yes.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:34.360
Why did you do that?

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:35.850
The Omni Berkshire Hotel.

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:36.683
[Conan] Mm-hmm.

00:02:36.683 --> 00:02:39.960
Because I was, I was having a...

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:41.330
I was a Duran Durani.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:42.610
I was a Durani fan.

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:45.637
And they were doing Saturday Night Live

00:02:45.637 --> 00:02:46.900
and they were the musical guest.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:50.080
And you know, they say,
"Tonight's guests for, you know,

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.100
whatever, are staying at
the Omni Berkshire Hotel."

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.550
No, they're not.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:54.740
And I... (audience laughs)

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:58.210
with my girlfriends went out with a rose

00:02:58.210 --> 00:02:59.950
and waited for them to come home,

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.180
and they never came home.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.070
And so we stayed out there all night.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.090
I didn't actually sleep
That's so sad.

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:05.627
on the street, that's
a little pathetic, but.

00:03:05.627 --> 00:03:06.880
Right, right.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.520
I do that, I sleep on the street.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:09.353
You do?

00:03:09.353 --> 00:03:10.186
When Mr. T is in town-

00:03:10.186 --> 00:03:11.019
Even now?

00:03:11.019 --> 00:03:11.852
And I know where he's
staying. (audience laughs)

00:03:11.852 --> 00:03:12.685
You do?

00:03:12.685 --> 00:03:15.440
No, I understand though,
that level of intensity

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.960
about I really want to meet this person.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:19.330
It was really weird of me, I have to say.

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:21.000
It's a little strange phase.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.360
But one thing that's
nice is then you go on

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:24.930
and become a big star, you could meet,

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:25.916
have you ever met

00:03:25.916 --> 00:03:26.749
the people from Duran Duran?
Yes I have.

00:03:26.749 --> 00:03:28.510
I met Simon Le Bon.

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:29.343
[Conan] Oh, you did?

00:03:29.343 --> 00:03:30.970
Yeah, I think I scared him actually.

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:31.803
What happened?

00:03:31.803 --> 00:03:33.450
Well, I was with a friend of mine

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:37.220
at a store in Santa Monica.

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:41.500
And my friend saw him and
just basically grabbed him

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:43.360
and said, "Don't move.
You just stay right here.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:44.193
Don't move."

00:03:44.193 --> 00:03:45.297
And ran and got me and was like,

00:03:45.297 --> 00:03:46.310
"Jen, you've gotta come here.

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:47.700
You've got to see this.
You've got to see this."

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.550
So I think I'm gonna see
something, not someone.

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:53.190
And he basically throws me and I just,

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:55.207
I just, I couldn't believe it.

00:03:55.207 --> 00:03:56.070
And I told him, I said,

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:58.055
I slept out in front of a hotel for you.

00:03:58.055 --> 00:03:58.888
(Conan laughs)

00:03:58.888 --> 00:03:59.721
He didn't say a word.

00:03:59.721 --> 00:04:00.840
I mean, he literally didn't speak.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.945
I think we just scared him
and he didn't say anything.

00:04:02.945 --> 00:04:04.665
But were you known?

00:04:04.665 --> 00:04:05.498
Were you famous Jennifer Aniston then?

00:04:05.498 --> 00:04:06.331
Yes.

00:04:06.331 --> 00:04:07.740
So I can't believe he
didn't say, "Oh my God.

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:08.800
That's so..." I mean, you know?

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:10.710
No, he just sort of slowly looked at me

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:13.010
like I was nuts and grabbed
my hand and shook it

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.390
and then we... it was
a very awkward moment.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:16.832
I don't really remember it truthfully.

00:04:16.832 --> 00:04:18.642
Yeah, yeah. (audience laughs)

00:04:18.642 --> 00:04:19.650
I think you blacked out.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:20.734
I think that's what happened.

00:04:20.734 --> 00:04:21.567
I may have.

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:22.400
Yeah.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.480
And you had a traumatic experience

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:25.430
here in New York City
involving Santa Claus.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:26.810
Santa slapped me.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.331
What? (audience laughs)

00:04:28.331 --> 00:04:29.164
This is good.

00:04:29.164 --> 00:04:31.830
It was a homeless guy
wearing a Santa's hat.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:32.700
[Conan] Right.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:36.070
And I was walking down
Broadway after a dance class

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:37.510
and I was with my girlfriend

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.230
and I basically saw this guy standing

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:40.063
in the middle of the street

00:04:40.063 --> 00:04:42.340
and I just happened to be
passing him right at the time

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:43.980
that he just went-

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:44.813
[Conan] Oh my God.

00:04:44.813 --> 00:04:45.646
And backhanded me-

00:04:45.646 --> 00:04:46.479
[Conan] Right, right.

00:04:46.479 --> 00:04:47.312
Really hard.

00:04:47.312 --> 00:04:48.145
[Conan] Yeah.

00:04:48.145 --> 00:04:48.978
And I was stunned, and I was like,

00:04:48.978 --> 00:04:49.811
"What the hell are you doing?"

00:04:49.811 --> 00:04:51.630
And nobody stopped and...

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:53.060
I don't know what you expect people to do.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:56.860
Like go beat up the homeless
Santa. (Conan laughs)

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:57.940
Yes, yes.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.310
Something! But there was no, you know.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:00.216
See, that's New York.

00:05:00.216 --> 00:05:01.049
People are just like,
It's very strange.

00:05:01.049 --> 00:05:02.038
"Yeah, girl got hit by Santa."
Yeah, whatever.

00:05:02.038 --> 00:05:02.871
That happens all the time.

00:05:02.871 --> 00:05:04.473
Let's go, you know? (audience laughs)

00:05:04.473 --> 00:05:05.306
So.

00:05:05.306 --> 00:05:06.139
Yeah, so.

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:07.280
It's fun growing up in New York.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.050
Yeah, these are heart
warming stories, yeah.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:09.883
Aren't they great? (audience laughs)

00:05:09.883 --> 00:05:11.920
I can tell you that the
muggings too, that was fun.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:12.753
Now let's talk about,

00:05:12.753 --> 00:05:13.790
let's talk about Derailed

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:15.357
because I got to see this movie last night

00:05:15.357 --> 00:05:16.640
and I really liked it.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:17.620
And I don't...

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:18.970
It's a very difficult movie to talk about

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:19.803
'cause you can-

00:05:19.803 --> 00:05:20.665
Yes.

00:05:20.665 --> 00:05:21.498
Give some things away.

00:05:21.498 --> 00:05:22.331
So I'm not going to do that.

00:05:22.331 --> 00:05:23.164
Great.

00:05:23.164 --> 00:05:24.760
It's a suspenseful thriller
with lots of twists.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:25.593
Yes.

00:05:25.593 --> 00:05:28.270
Xzibit is in this movie.
He's one of your co-stars,

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:30.120
and he was on the show the other day.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.130
And he said it was hard for him

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.130
because the first day on the set,

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:35.850
literally, the first thing he had to do

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:36.683
as part of his character

00:05:36.683 --> 00:05:38.300
was grab you and put a gun to your head

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:39.390
and sort of throw you around.

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:40.750
And he said he was freaked out.

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:41.583
Yeah, he was.

00:05:41.583 --> 00:05:42.660
He just really didn't
want to do that to you.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:43.757
He really didn't.

00:05:43.757 --> 00:05:45.310
And he was so sweet.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:46.610
He just kept apologizing.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:47.730
And, "Are you okay? Are you okay?"

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:48.563
to the point where I was like,

00:05:48.563 --> 00:05:50.163
"You really just got to throw me down."

00:05:50.163 --> 00:05:51.390
(audience laughs)

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:52.800
You just don't... I mean, I'm okay.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:54.510
I'll let you know if it hurts.

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:55.900
Right, Right.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:56.739
I could see...

00:05:56.739 --> 00:05:59.650
(laughing)

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:02.023
Moving on. (audience laughs)

00:06:02.023 --> 00:06:03.054
Back to Santa.

00:06:03.054 --> 00:06:03.887
Yeah.

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:06.820
It's them, It's not us.

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:08.356
No, it just sounded strange.

00:06:08.356 --> 00:06:09.693
They're dirty people.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:14.000
You're working with, this
is a Swedish director.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:14.833
Swedish.

00:06:14.833 --> 00:06:15.860
Swedish, a Swedish director.

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:17.070
Yeah.

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:20.040
Did you learn any cool Swedish terms?

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:20.873
Swedish words.

00:06:20.873 --> 00:06:21.706
Yeah.

00:06:21.706 --> 00:06:22.930
He did teach us a couple.

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:25.500
It's hard to remember
the Swedish language.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.333
[Conan] Right.

00:06:26.333 --> 00:06:27.166
But-

00:06:27.166 --> 00:06:27.999
People remember the cadence.

00:06:27.999 --> 00:06:28.832
They remember the hida, hada, hooda, hida.

00:06:28.832 --> 00:06:30.047
They remember the cadence, exactly.

00:06:30.047 --> 00:06:31.120
Right, right.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:33.330
And he doesn't really talk
like that at all, actually,

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:34.920
that's not really the way they talk.

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:36.250
Right, right.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.506
I like my stereotypes though.

00:06:37.506 --> 00:06:38.630
Do you? So do I. (audience laughs)

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:40.106
Let's just put them in a box.
Irish people are like,

00:06:40.106 --> 00:06:41.555
♪ Hoo dee hi dee di dee ho ♪

00:06:41.555 --> 00:06:42.388
(audience laughs)

00:06:42.388 --> 00:06:43.510
It's just much simpler that way.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:44.970
Yeah. (chuckles)

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.250
No, he's... I don't know if it's canoodle.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:48.083
Canoodle.

00:06:48.083 --> 00:06:49.320
There are certain words
that you just start to...

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:50.270
I don't think-

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:51.493
Canoodle is a Swedish word I guess.

00:06:51.493 --> 00:06:52.326
Canoodla.

00:06:52.326 --> 00:06:53.159
Yeah.

00:06:53.159 --> 00:06:53.992
Isn't it? Canoodla? Canoodle.

00:06:53.992 --> 00:06:55.600
But you know, then you
start using it for anything,

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.380
like don't you get canoodle-y with me.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:58.320
What's funny, they also use it

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:00.390
in the tabloids all the time.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.100
They're always talking about celebrities

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.580
were seen canoodling in a bar.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:04.413
Yes.

00:07:04.413 --> 00:07:06.865
And I think it's such a,
it's such a weird term.

00:07:06.865 --> 00:07:07.865
It's a good word though,
isn't it? It's fun.

00:07:07.865 --> 00:07:09.285
It sounds like they're
just making pasta together

00:07:09.285 --> 00:07:11.250
or something.
I know. (laughs)

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:14.850
My mom, and this is
true, If two people are,

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:18.990
you know, getting busy, she
calls it playing patty fingers.

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:19.823
[Jennifer] Oh.

00:07:19.823 --> 00:07:21.160
She's like, "Oh, I heard he was playing

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:22.130
patty fingers with her."

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:24.140
And I'm like, what are you talking about?

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:26.600
They get together and go heeeeee?

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:27.620
The dumbest thing in the world.

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:29.210
That sounds strange.

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:30.410
She's a strange woman.

